# fixedbugs, defect 151, lane land186, 2026-10-02 (panel 186 R2).
#
# SYMPTOM: a record over a struct holding an anonymous union, naming both of
# its arms, was built at exit 0, `SA(kind: 1, i: 7, f: 0.5, x: 3).i` printing
# 1056964608, the bits of 0.5, with clang's *excess elements* and *initializer
# overrides* warnings on the author's lines.
#
# CAUSE: the union rule asked C whether the TYPE was a union
# (`__builtin_classify_type`, panel 077), and a struct holding one answers
# struct; nothing asked whether two declared fields are one union's bytes.
#
# FIX: the header's layout is read from clang (`cli/layout.hero`), and building
# a record whose two declared fields share bytes is refused at `build`, by C's
# own offsets and sizes. Reading through both stays legal.
#
# **Moved 2026-10-02, panel 186 R7** (lane land186, the author's *2a*): a
# record over a C union names one or more of each union's members, reads any,
# and is built naming exactly one, so `record SA` naming both arms is legal and
# the refusal is the construction's, told at it with the two arms it names
# (`emit/layout_sites.hero`, `emit/ffi_built.hero`). Until R7 it was told on
# the record's line.

extern "fixedbugs-151-unions.h"
    record SA
        kind: i32
        i: i32
        f: f32
        x: i32

function main()
    s = SA(kind: 1, i: 7, f: 0.5, x: 3)  #~ ffi_union_field
    print(s.i)
